      noAnswerSubtitle: "Send us an email and we'll reply as soon as possible.",
      questions: [
        { q: "Do I need to upload my photos somewhere?", a: "No. Your photos stay exactly where they are, in your Google Drive. PhotoDrive reads them from there and displays them to your client. You don't need to do anything again." },
        { q: "How does my client view the gallery?", a: "Once you create a gallery, PhotoDrive automatically generates a unique link (e.g. yourdomain.com/gallery/123456789). You send it to your client via email, SMS, or wherever you want. Your client opens the link and sees the gallery immediately, no sign-up, no account needed." },
        { q: "Can I add a password to the gallery?", a: "Yes. When creating a gallery you can set a password. Your client will need to enter it before viewing the photos. The password is stored encrypted and cannot be revealed by anyone." },
        { q: "Does my client need a Google account to view the gallery?", a: "No. Your client doesn't need any account. They simply open the link you sent and see the gallery. If there's a password, they only need to enter that." },
        { q: "Can my client download the photos?", a: "Yes. Your client can download individual photos in full resolution directly from the gallery. They can also select multiple photos and download them all together as a ZIP file." },
        { q: "What happens if I add or remove photos from Google Drive?", a: "The gallery updates automatically. If you add photos to the Drive folder, they'll appear in the gallery. If you remove photos, they won't show anymore. You don't need to do anything in PhotoDrive." },
        { q: "How many galleries can I create?", a: "Unlimited. Your subscription has no limit on the number of galleries or photos." },
        { q: "What file types are supported?", a: "PhotoDrive supports all common image formats (JPEG, PNG, WebP, HEIC, etc.) as well as videos (MP4, MOV, etc.). The files just need to be in the Drive folder you selected." },
        { q: "Are my photos safe?", a: "PhotoDrive has exclusively read-only access to the Drive folder you choose. We don't store your photos anywhere. We don't modify or delete anything in your Drive. Data transfer always happens over HTTPS." },
        { q: "What if the Drive folder is not public?", a: 'For the gallery to work, the Drive folder must be set so that "Anyone with the link" can view it. This doesn\'t mean your folder appears on Google, it simply means PhotoDrive can read the files.' },
        { q: "What devices does PhotoDrive work on?", a: "PhotoDrive works on every modern browser, Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Edge, on desktop, tablet, and mobile. No app installation needed." },
      ],
